{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector/pulls/15993","id":4595223982,"node_id":"PR_kwDOCxQENc8AAAABEeWNrg","html_url":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector/pull/15993","diff_url":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector/pull/15993.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector/pull/15993.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector/issues/15993","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector/pulls/15993/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector/pulls/15993/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector/issues/15993/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector/statuses/b930d34a4f7f3f7acb0cf79c02e0372d09e06a88","number":15993,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[POC] implement a direct disk access queue to speed up persistent queue","user":{"login":"atoulme","id":16758,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzU4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16758?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atoulme","html_url":"https://github.com/atoulme","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atoulme/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atoulme/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atoulme/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atoulme/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atoulme/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atoulme/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atoulme/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atoulme/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atoulme/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<!--Ex. Fixing a bug - Describe the bug and how this fixes the issue.\r\nEx. Adding a feature - Explain what this achieves.-->\r\n#### Description\r\nThis POC is a complete implementation of a queue backed by direct disk access.\r\n\r\nIt is made of 3 components:\r\n* A queue interface similar to the storage interface for components to request Clients that allow access to the queue\r\n* A change to the persistent queue to allow to use this interface (hacky workaround for now)\r\n* A reference implementation that uses a set of rotating files to store queue data\r\n\r\n<!-- Issue number if applicable -->\r\n#### Link to tracking issue\r\nRelates to #15384\r\n\r\n<!--Describe what testing was performed and which tests were added.-->\r\n#### Testing\r\nUnit testing throughout - pardon the agentic mess. Also ran benchmarks.\r\n\r\n<!--Describe the documentation added.-->\r\n#### Documentation\r\nSome documentation in code. We might like to add a few more README entries.\r\n\r\n<!--Authorship attestation. See AGENTS.md for details. AI agents must not check this box on behalf\r\nof the user; the human author must check it themselves before the PR is ready for review.-->\r\n#### Authorship\r\n\r\n- [x] I, a human, wrote this pull request description myself.\r\n\r\n<!--Please delete paragraphs that you did not use before submitting.-->\r\n\r\n\r\n#### Performance benchmarks\r\nI had Claude create a performance benchmark and compare to bbolt-backed file storage:\r\n\r\nHere's the comparison, per 100 offer+consume operations (each b.Loop() iteration):\r\n\r\n\r\n│ Queue │  ns/op  │  B/op │ allocs/op │\r\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\r\n│ Memory                                           │ ~38,700        │ 4,900     │ 100       │\r\n│ Persistent (mock/in-memory storage)              │ ~83,800        │ 96,800    │ 3,116     │\r\n│ Disk (diskaccess extension, real files)          │ ~1,230,000     │ 15,130    │ 503       │\r\n│ Persistent (real filestorage/bbolt, FSync: true) │ ~2,263,500,000 │ 8,175,000 │ 14,582    │\r\n\r\n\r\nTakeaways:\r\n  - With a real bbolt-backed filestorage extension and FSync: true, persistent queue drops from ~84µs/op to ~2.26 seconds/op — roughly 27,000x slower than the mock, and ~1,800x slower than the disk queue. This is fsync()-per-transaction cost: bbolt does a full durable commit (fsync + page writes) for every Batch call, and each Offer/consume does one.\r\n  - Disk queue vs real filestorage is now the fair comparison you were after: disk queue (~1.23ms/op) is ~1,840x faster than fsync'd bbolt (~2,263ms/op) for the same 100-op batch, because diskaccess's writer only calls Sync() periodically (every SyncEvery writes / SyncTimeout tick) rather than fsync-ing on every single write like bbolt's transactional model does.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-21T19:18:43Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T15:57:15Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"bogdandrutu","id":1373887,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzM4ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1373887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bogdandrutu","html_url":"https://github.com/bogdandrutu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bogdandrutu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bogdandrutu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bogdandrutu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bogdandrutu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bogdandrutu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bogdandrutu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bogdandrutu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bogdandrutu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"http